{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S9SvuZBZPYYGxh4ZhQJWdv","type":"tool_result","content":"100\t        on_invalid_state:\n101\t          halt: true\n102\t          release_lock: step_release_lock\n103\t          message: \"Existing deep-review state in review/ is incomplete or contradictory. Repair or archive the invalid review packet before continuing.\"\n104\t        on_fresh:\n105\t          action: \"Proceed with a new session\"\n106\t\n107\t      step_scope_discovery:\n108\t        action: \"Resolve review target to a concrete file list based on target type\"\n109\t        pre_bound: \"When review_scope_file is bound, as a fan-out lineage's setup binds it, set review_scope_files to that file's lines in order and skip the resolve rules below: the fan-out root already discovered the scope every lineage shares.\"\n110\t        resolve:\n111\t          spec-folder: |\n112\t            1. Inspect spec.md, plan.md, tasks.md, acceptance-criteria.md, implementation-summary.md, and goal-file-manifest.txt when present\n113\t            2. If goal-file-manifest.txt exists, parse one repo-relative path per non-empty, non-comment line; reject absolute paths, traversal outside repo_root, duplicates, missing paths, and non-file entries\n114\t            3. Fail before dispatch with line-numbered validation errors when any manifest entry is invalid; otherwise set scope = the validated manifest paths in declared order\n115\t            4. When no manifest exists, discover implementation files referenced in the canonical spec artifacts\n116\t            5. Discover test files associated with the implementation files\n117\t            6. Set scope = the packet's own canonical docs plus all discovered implementation and test files\n118\t          skill: |\n119\t            1. Read SKILL.md from .skilled/skills/{skill_name}/\n120\t            2. Discover references/, assets/, scripts/ contents\n121\t            3. Find agent definitions referencing this skill across runtimes\n122\t            4. Find command entry points referencing this skill\n123\t            5. Set scope = all discovered files\n124\t          agent: |\n125\t            1. Find agent definition across repo-managed runtimes (.claude/agents/, .skilled/agents/)\n126\t            2. Compare agent definitions for consistency\n127\t            3. Set scope = all discovered agent files\n128\t          track: |\n129\t            1. List all child spec folders under specs/{track}/ or .opencode/specs/{track}/\n130\t            2. For each: read spec.md + acceptance-criteria.md\n131\t            3. Set scope = all child spec artifacts\n132\t          files: |\n133\t            1. Expand glob patterns from review_target\n134\t            2. Validate all files exist\n135\t            3. Discover immediate cross-references (imports, links)\n136\t            4. Set scope = expanded file list + cross-references\n137\t        outputs:\n138\t          - review_scope_files: \"List of all files in review scope\"\n139\t          - cross_reference_targets: \"{ spec_paths: [...], code_paths: [...], test_paths: [...] }\"\n140\t\n141\t      step_order_dimensions:\n142\t        action: \"Order review dimensions based on risk priority\"\n143\t        algorithm: |\n144\t          1. Iteration 0 (inventory pass): Build artifact map, identify file types, estimate complexity\n145\t          2. Subsequent iterations follow risk-ordered deep passes:\n146\t             correctness → security → traceability → maintainability\n147\t          3. If review_dimensions != \"all\", filter to only requested dimensions; each configured custom dimension follows the canonical four, in configured order\n148\t          4. Derive traceability protocol plan:\n149\t             - core: spec_code, checklist_evidence\n150\t             - overlay: skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability\n151\t          5. If resource_map_present, reserve at least one traceability-oriented pass to cross-check target_files from applied/T-*.md against resource-map.md and classify touched / expected-by-scope / gap / absent-from-map outcomes\n152\t          6. Store ordered list as dimension_queue\n153\t        outputs:\n154\t          - dimension_queue: \"Ordered list of dimensions to review\"\n155\t          - inventory_pass: true\n156\t\n157\t      step_normalize_review_dimensions:\n158\t        action: \"Normalize reviewDimensions once during init for config + JSONL reuse\"\n159\t        outputs:\n160\t          - review_dimensions_normalized: \"Canonical string[] for deep-review-config.json\"\n161\t          - review_dimensions_json: \"JSON.stringify(review_dimensions_normalized) for JSONL config record\"\n162\t          - review_dimensions_list: \"The canonical four in risk order, then each configured custom dimension in configured order, joined by ', '\"\n163\t          - dimension_coverage_custom_seed: \"For each configured custom dimension in configured order, the text ,\\\"<name>\\\":false; empty when every configured dimension is canonical\"\n164\t        normalize: |\n165\t          Accept {review_dimensions} in any of these shapes and convert once:\n166\t            - \"all\" → [\"correctness\",\"security\",\"traceability\",\"maintainability\"]\n167\t            - \"correctness,security\" → [\"correctness\",\"security\"]\n168\t            - [\"correctness\"] → [\"correctness\"]\n169\t            - \"correctness,performance\" → [\"correctness\",\"performance\"]\n170\t          Trim and lowercase each element and drop duplicates; an empty name fails setup. A name outside the four canonical dimension names is a custom dimension, kept in configured order after the canonical ones.\n171\t\n172\t      step_normalize_review_focus:\n173\t        action: \"Normalize the optional operator review focus once during init\"\n174\t        outputs:\n175\t          - review_focus_normalized: \"Single-line focus text, or empty string when no focus was given\"\n176\t        normalize: |\n177\t          Collapse every control character (C0, C1, DEL, U+2028, U+2029) and whitespace run to one space, trim, treat an empty result as absent, and fail setup when more than 1000 characters remain.\n178\t          fanout-run.cjs applies the same rule in code, so a fan-out lineage receives the same text.\n179\t\n180\t      step_resolve_session_id:\n181\t        action: \"Resolve init session id from caller when supplied, else preserve timestamp fallback\"\n182\t        branch_on: \"session_id\"\n183\t        if_present:\n184\t          bind:\n185\t            session_id_init: \"{session_id}\"\n186\t        if_absent:\n187\t          bind:\n188\t            session_id_init: \"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"\n189\t\n190\t      step_create_config:\n191\t        action: \"Create deep-review-config.json from template with review-specific fields\"\n192\t        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n193\t        template: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json\n194\t        lineage_values:\n195\t          generation_init: \"{prior_generation + 1} when lineage_mode == 'restart', else 1\"\n196\t          lineage_mode_init: \"restart when lineage_mode == 'restart', else new\"\n197\t          parent_session_id_init: \"{prior_session_id} when lineage_mode == 'restart', else null\"\n198\t        populate:\n199\t          topic: \"Review: {review_target}\"\n200\t          mode: \"review\"\n201\t          sessionId: \"{session_id_init}\"\n202\t          parentSessionId: \"{parent_session_id_init}\"\n203\t          lineageMode: \"{lineage_mode_init}\"\n204\t          generation: \"{generation_init}\"\n205\t          continuedFromRun: null\n206\t          reviewTarget: \"{review_target}\"\n207\t          reviewTargetType: \"{review_target_type}\"\n208\t          # Reuse the single normalized init-time value from step_normalize_review_dimensions.\n209\t          reviewDimensions: \"{review_dimensions_normalized}\"\n210\t          # Null when review_focus_normalized is empty. The review report reads it back to show the focus.\n211\t          reviewFocus: \"{review_focus_normalized}\"\n212\t          resource_map_present: \"{resource_map_present}\"\n213\t          reviewScopeFiles: \"{review_scope_files}\"\n214\t          severityThreshold: \"P2\"\n215\t          crossReference:\n216\t            core: [\"spec_code\", \"checklist_evidence\"]\n217\t            overlay: [\"skill_agent\", \"agent_cross_runtime\", \"feature_catalog_code\", \"playbook_capability\"]\n218\t          maxIterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n219\t          # Semantic: weighted P0/P1/P2 severity ratio. See SKILL.md §\"Convergence Threshold Semantics\".\n220\t          convergenceThreshold: \"{convergence_threshold}\"\n221\t          antiConvergence.convergenceMode: \"{convergence_mode}\"\n222\t          antiConvergence.depthMode: \"{depth_mode}\"\n223\t          # Written as a JSON integer: frontier-admit.cjs reads a quoted number as unset and falls back to the default.\n224\t          expansiveDepth.maxDepth: \"{frontier_max_depth} when bound, else 3\"\n225\t          expansiveDepth.maxChildrenPerNode: 6\n226\t          expansiveDepth.budgetSplit: { depth1: 0.5, depth2: 0.35, depth3: 0.15 }\n227\t          # Null derives the run-wide node cap at admission as half the iteration budget, so the frontier cannot claim every iteration; the depth-1 seed answers only to the root-children cap but counts toward this one. A defaulted budget is resized from the seed by step_frontier_budget so the cap keeps room past depth 1; an explicit budget is kept as given and may leave none.\n228\t          expansiveDepth.maxFrontierNodes: \"{frontier_max_nodes} when bound, else null\"\n229\t          antiConvergence.divergent: {}\n230\t          stopPolicy: \"{stop_policy}\"\n231\t          stuckThreshold: 2\n232\t          maxDurationMinutes: 120\n233\t          specFolder: \"{spec_folder}\"\n234\t          # Honor the parsed --no-resource-map flag from deep-review.md:71 (default true; false when flag is set).\n235\t          # The markdown command parses $ARGUMENTS and binds {resource_map_emit} before this step runs.\n236\t          resource_map.emit: \"{resource_map_emit}\"\n237\t          createdAt: \"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"\n238\t          status: \"initialized\"\n239\t          releaseReadinessState: \"in-progress\"\n240\t          executionMode: \"{execution_mode}\"\n241\t        output: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n242\t\n243\t      step_frontier_scope:\n244\t        description: \"Record the files a commit-range target touches before admission reads them\"\n245\t        enabled_when: \"depth_mode == 'expansive'\"\n246\t        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n247\t        note: |\n248\t          Relevance and the terminal scope gate read reviewScopeFiles, and for a\n249\t          commit-range target only git knows those files. The command replaces the\n250\t          list step_scope_discovery recorded with git diff --name-only <range> --\n251\t          <pathspec>, the pathspec being the paths after '--' up to a parenthesized\n252\t          label, and leaves any other target untouched. A fan-out lineage runs it\n253\t          too, after its own step_create_config, so its list is the same as every\n254\t          other lineage's. A default-mode run never reaches this step.\n255\t        command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs scope --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\"'\n256\t        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n257\t        outputs:\n258\t          - frontier_scope_json: \"The JSON line the command prints: touchedFiles, range and pathspec, or skipped\"\n259\t        on_failure: \"Halt with the command's stderr line. Admission must not run against a guessed file list.\"\n260\t\n261\t      step_frontier_seed:\n262\t        description: \"Seed the depth-1 review frontier so iteration 1 already has open nodes\"\n263\t        enabled_when: \"depth_mode == 'expansive'\"\n264\t        skip_when: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n265\t        skip_reason: \"A fan-out lineage receives its share of the parent's seeded nodes from fanout-run.cjs; seeding again would duplicate them.\"\n266\t        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n267\t        instructions: |\n268\t          Decompose {review_target} and write {artifact_dir}/frontier-seed.json\n269\t          exactly as the root step_frontier_seed describes, then run the command.\n270\t          The decomposition is defined once, there; this call site exists because\n271\t          a fan-out run seeds before phase_init and a single-executor run seeds\n272\t          only once its config exists.\n273\t        command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs seed --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\" --iteration 0 --input \"{artifact_dir}/frontier-seed.json\" --max-iterations-source \"{max_iterations_source}\"'\n274\t        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n275\t        outputs:\n276\t          - frontier_seed_json: \"The JSON line the command prints: admitted node ids and pruned {nodeId, reason} rows\"\n277\t        on_failure: \"Halt with the command's stderr line. A run that asked for expansive depth must not start without its seeded frontier.\"\n278\t\n279\t      step_frontier_budget:\n280\t        description: \"Size a defaulted expansive budget from the seed before the loop reads max_iterations\"\n281\t        enabled_when: \"depth_mode == 'expansive' and max_iterations_source == 'default'\"\n282\t        skip_when: \"extension_pending == true or config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n283\t        skip_reason: \"An explicit budget always wins, an extension already set its own budget, and a fan-out lineage gets its budget from fanout-run.cjs.\"\n284\t        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n285\t        note: |\n286\t          The seed decides how many nodes the frontier starts with, so a defaulted budget\n287\t          is sized only now: min(24, max(loop default, 2 x c x (seeded nodes + maxDepth - 1))),\n288\t          where c is 1 for research and, for review, the four canonical dimensions less\n289\t          traceability when the configured reviewDimensions list leaves it out, plus any\n290\t          custom name, each counted once. With no seeded node, every seed pruned,\n291\t          the budget stays at the loop default. The node cap stays half the final budget.\n292\t          A default-mode run never reaches this step, so its config gains no key.\n293\t        command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs budget --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\"'\n294\t        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n295\t        outputs:\n296\t          - max_iterations: \"derivedMaxIterations from the JSON output; it replaces the command default so the loop cap, the strategy and the convergence script read the same ceiling\"\n297\t          - frontier_growth_slots: \"growthSlots from the JSON output\"\n298\t        on_success: \"Print 'Expansive budget: <derivedMaxIterations> iterations, <growthSlots> growth slots past depth 1', and print the warning when the output carries one.\"\n299\t        on_failure: \"Halt with the command's stderr line. The config keeps the defaulted budget.\"\n300\t\n301\t      step_create_state_log:\n302\t        action: \"Open the run in the ledger: record deep_review.run_initialized through the append gateway, which writes the state log's first row\"\n303\t        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n304\t        note: |\n305\t          The state log is a projection the gateway rebuilds from the ledger, so this step never writes\n306\t          it directly. A config row written beside the ledger carries keys the projection cannot\n307\t          rebuild, and the projection refuses to drop them, so every later append in the run would\n308\t          commit to the ledger and then exit 2. Recording the run's opening as a ledger event makes\n309\t          the projected config row the state log's first row from the start. The full config stays\n310\t          in deep-review-config.json, which is what the reducer reads.\n311\t        command: |\n312\t          GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n313\t          [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n314\t          EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-run-open.XXXXXX\")\"\n315\t          node \"$(dirname \"$GATEWAY\")/workflow-steps.cjs\" run-open-review \"{state_paths.config}\" \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml\" > \"$EVENT_FILE\" || { rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"; exit 1; }\n316\t          node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n317\t          STATUS=$?\n318\t          rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n319\t          exit \"$STATUS\"\n320\t        output: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n321\t\n322\t      step_record_restarted_run:\n323\t        skip_when: \"lineage_mode != 'restart'\"\n324\t        action: \"Record the restarted lineage after the run-open row so the restart marker never precedes deep_review.run_initialized\"\n325\t        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n326\t        append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.run_restarted\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}},\"data\":{\"priorTailDigest\":\"{prior_tail_digest}\",\"archivedLineageId\":\"{prior_session_id}\",\"restartReason\":\"Restart requested: the prior review packet was archived and a new lineage segment opened.\",\"continuedFromRunId\":\"{prior_session_id}-i{iteration_count}\",\"compatibilityDecision\":\"exact\",\"recoveryReceiptRef\":\"none\"}}'\n327\t\n328\t      step_create_findings_registry:\n329\t        action: \"Initialize reducer-owned review findings registry\"\n330\t        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n331\t        content: '{\"sessionId\":\"{session_id_init}\",\"generation\":{generation_init},\"lineageMode\":\"{lineage_mode_init}\",\"openFindings\":[],\"resolvedFindings\":[],\"repeatedFindings\":[],\"dimensionCoverage\":{\"correctness\":false,\"security\":false,\"traceability\":false,\"maintainability\":false{dimension_coverage_custom_seed}},\"findingsBySeverity\":{\"P0\":0,\"P1\":0,\"P2\":0},\"openFindingsCount\":0,\"resolvedFindingsCount\":0,\"convergenceScore\":0.0}'\n332\t        output: \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n333\t\n334\t      step_create_strategy:\n335\t        action: \"Create review strategy file from deep-review-strategy.md template\"\n336\t        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n337\t        template: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md\n338\t        populate:\n339\t          review_target: \"{review_target}\"\n340\t          review_target_type: \"{review_target_type}\"\n341\t          dimensions: \"{dimension_queue}\"\n342\t          scope_files: \"{review_scope_files}\"\n343\t          cross_reference_targets: \"{cross_reference_targets}\"\n344\t          max_iterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n345\t          convergence_threshold: \"{convergence_threshold}\"\n346\t          stop_policy: \"{stop_policy}\"\n347\t        output: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n348\t\n349\t      step_seed_coverage_graph:\n350\t        action: \"Seed the review coverage graph before the first convergence check\"\n351\t        fanout_graph_store: 'When config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID is set, this run is a fan-out lineage and its coverage graph store is {artifact_dir}/graph-db, inside the lineage write surface. The fan-out runner exports DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR to that directory. Run this step against it and never skip it as a write outside the lineage; when DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR is absent from the environment, prefix the command with DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR=\"{artifact_dir}/graph-db\".'\n352\t        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n353\t        transform: |\n354\t          1. Convert review_scope_files into FILE nodes.\n355\t          2. Convert review target groupings into coarse SLICE nodes only; do not expand SYMBOL\n356\t             or DEPENDENCY nodes in review mode.\n357\t          3. Emit COVERS edges from SLICE nodes to FILE nodes when the grouping is known.\n358\t          4. Bind coverage_seed_source to \"scope_discovery\" and coverage_seed_confidence to 0.50.\n359\t          5. When scope discovery yields no files, emit [] for both arrays; the upsert script\n360\t             returns a warning and review continues with an empty graph.\n361\t        bash: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs --spec-folder \\\"{spec_folder}\\\" --loop-type \\\"review\\\" --session-id \\\"{config.sessionId}\\\" --nodes '{coverage_seed_nodes_json}' --edges '{coverage_seed_edges_json}' --seed-source \\\"{coverage_seed_source}\\\" --seed-confidence \\\"{coverage_seed_confidence}\\\"\"\n362\t        outputs:\n363\t          - coverage_seed_nodes_json: \"Seed nodes for review SLICE and FILE kinds only\"\n364\t          - coverage_seed_edges_json: \"Seed COVERS edges where review target groupings resolved\"\n365\t          - coverage_seed_warning: \"Warning emitted when the seed batch inserts zero nodes, else empty\"\n366\t        on_warning:\n367\t          log: \"Coverage graph seed inserted zero nodes; continuing with an empty graph.\"\n368\t          proceed: true\n369\t\n370\t      step_enrich_strategy_context:\n371\t        action: \"Ensure Known Context is written only after strategy.md exists\"\n372\t        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n373\t        condition: \"prior_context_found\"\n374\t        edit: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n375\t        note: \"Append or replace the Known Context section with prior_context_summary and retained detail from prior_context\"\n376\t\n377\t      step_enrich_strategy_resource_map:\n378\t        action: \"Inject resource-map status into Known Context after strategy.md exists\"\n379\t        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n380\t        edit: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n381\t        note: \"When resource_map_present is true, append the resource_map_known_context snapshot and add Resource Map Coverage to the Review Charter. When false, append 'resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate'.\"\n382\t\n383\t      step_frontier_reduce_seed:\n384\t        action: \"Reduce once after the seed so iteration 1 already reviews a frontier node\"\n385\t        enabled_when: \"depth_mode == 'expansive'\"\n386\t        dry_run_boundary: \"reducer-refresh\"\n387\t        note: \"The loop binds active_frontier_node and the frontier dimension from registry.frontier, and step_create_findings_registry writes a registry with no frontier after the seed has run. Only the reducer projects the seeded nodes into it. Without this pass the first iteration has no frontier node and no frontier block. A fan-out lineage runs it too: its reducer_artifact_arg points the reducer at the lineage's own directory, where fanout-run.cjs put its share of the nodes.\"\n388\t        command: |\n389\t          node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors\n390\t        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n391\t        on_failure: \"Log the stderr line as a config_warning bookkeeping event and continue; iteration 1 then runs on the strategy's own dimension queue and step_reduce_review_state picks the frontier up after it.\"\n392\t\n393\t      step_init_complete:\n394\t        log: \"Initialization complete. Config, state, and strategy files created. Review scope: {review_scope_files_count} files, {dimension_queue_count} dimensions.\"\n395\t        set: { current_iteration: 1, p0_count: 0, p1_count: 0, p2_count: 0 }\n396\t\n397\t      # ─── APPROVAL GATE: Post-Init ───\n398\t      gate_init_approval:\n399\t        applies_to: confirm\n400\t        type: approval_gate\n401\t        purpose: \"Show review scope, dimensions, and target files. Get approval to start loop.\"\n402\t        present: |\n403\t          ## Review Initialization Complete\n404\t\n405\t          **Review Target**: {review_target} ({review_target_type})\n406\t          **Scope**: {review_scope_files_count} files\n407\t          **Dimensions**: {dimension_queue}\n408\t          **Max Iterations**: {max_iterations}\n409\t          **Convergence Threshold**: {convergence_threshold}\n410\t          **Known Context Summary**: {prior_context_summary}\n411\t\n412\t          **Files in scope:**\n413\t          {review_scope_files_summary}\n414\t\n415\t          Review `{state_paths.strategy}` for the full scope and dimension ordering.\n416\t          **State files located in**: {state_paths.packet_dir}/\n417\t\n418\t          Options:\n419\t          A) Start review loop\n420\t          B) Adjust scope or dimensions\n421\t          C) Cancel\n422\t        wait_for: \"User response\"\n423\t        after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n424\t        on_A: { set: { current_iteration: 1, p0_count: 0, p1_count: 0, p2_count: 0 }, proceed_to: phase_loop }\n425\t        on_B: { action: \"Apply user adjustments to strategy.md, scope, or dimensions\", return_to: gate_init_approval }\n426\t        on_C: { action: \"Cancel workflow\", status: \"CANCELLED\", release_lock: step_release_lock }\n427\t\n428\t  # ════════\n429\t  # PHASE 2: ITERATION LOOP\n430\t  # ════════\n431\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:44:54.313Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/.claude-account2/projects/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/d8e266fe-4725-45c2-81f9-951ee232538e/tool-results/bxy17alut.txt","content":"        on_invalid_state:\n          halt: true\n          release_lock: step_release_lock\n          message: \"Existing deep-review state in review/ is incomplete or contradictory. Repair or archive the invalid review packet before continuing.\"\n        on_fresh:\n          action: \"Proceed with a new session\"\n\n      step_scope_discovery:\n        action: \"Resolve review target to a concrete file list based on target type\"\n        pre_bound: \"When review_scope_file is bound, as a fan-out lineage's setup binds it, set review_scope_files to that file's lines in order and skip the resolve rules below: the fan-out root already discovered the scope every lineage shares.\"\n        resolve:\n          spec-folder: |\n            1. Inspect spec.md, plan.md, tasks.md, acceptance-criteria.md, implementation-summary.md, and goal-file-manifest.txt when present\n            2. If goal-file-manifest.txt exists, parse one repo-relative path per non-empty, non-comment line; reject absolute paths, traversal outside repo_root, duplicates, missing paths, and non-file entries\n            3. Fail before dispatch with line-numbered validation errors when any manifest entry is invalid; otherwise set scope = the validated manifest paths in declared order\n            4. When no manifest exists, discover implementation files referenced in the canonical spec artifacts\n            5. Discover test files associated with the implementation files\n            6. Set scope = the packet's own canonical docs plus all discovered implementation and test files\n          skill: |\n            1. Read SKILL.md from .skilled/skills/{skill_name}/\n            2. Discover references/, assets/, scripts/ contents\n            3. Find agent definitions referencing this skill across runtimes\n            4. Find command entry points referencing this skill\n            5. Set scope = all discovered files\n          agent: |\n            1. Find agent definition across repo-managed runtimes (.claude/agents/, .skilled/agents/)\n            2. Compare agent definitions for consistency\n            3. Set scope = all discovered agent files\n          track: |\n            1. List all child spec folders under specs/{track}/ or .opencode/specs/{track}/\n            2. For each: read spec.md + acceptance-criteria.md\n            3. Set scope = all child spec artifacts\n          files: |\n            1. Expand glob patterns from review_target\n            2. Validate all files exist\n            3. Discover immediate cross-references (imports, links)\n            4. Set scope = expanded file list + cross-references\n        outputs:\n          - review_scope_files: \"List of all files in review scope\"\n          - cross_reference_targets: \"{ spec_paths: [...], code_paths: [...], test_paths: [...] }\"\n\n      step_order_dimensions:\n        action: \"Order review dimensions based on risk priority\"\n        algorithm: |\n          1. Iteration 0 (inventory pass): Build artifact map, identify file types, estimate complexity\n          2. Subsequent iterations follow risk-ordered deep passes:\n             correctness → security → traceability → maintainability\n          3. If review_dimensions != \"all\", filter to only requested dimensions; each configured custom dimension follows the canonical four, in configured order\n          4. Derive traceability protocol plan:\n             - core: spec_code, checklist_evidence\n             - overlay: skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability\n          5. If resource_map_present, reserve at least one traceability-oriented pass to cross-check target_files from applied/T-*.md against resource-map.md and classify touched / expected-by-scope / gap / absent-from-map outcomes\n          6. Store ordered list as dimension_queue\n        outputs:\n          - dimension_queue: \"Ordered list of dimensions to review\"\n          - inventory_pass: true\n\n      step_normalize_review_dimensions:\n        action: \"Normalize reviewDimensions once during init for config + JSONL reuse\"\n        outputs:\n          - review_dimensions_normalized: \"Canonical string[] for deep-review-config.json\"\n          - review_dimensions_json: \"JSON.stringify(review_dimensions_normalized) for JSONL config record\"\n          - review_dimensions_list: \"The canonical four in risk order, then each configured custom dimension in configured order, joined by ', '\"\n          - dimension_coverage_custom_seed: \"For each configured custom dimension in configured order, the text ,\\\"<name>\\\":false; empty when every configured dimension is canonical\"\n        normalize: |\n          Accept {review_dimensions} in any of these shapes and convert once:\n            - \"all\" → [\"correctness\",\"security\",\"traceability\",\"maintainability\"]\n            - \"correctness,security\" → [\"correctness\",\"security\"]\n            - [\"correctness\"] → [\"correctness\"]\n            - \"correctness,performance\" → [\"correctness\",\"performance\"]\n          Trim and lowercase each element and drop duplicates; an empty name fails setup. A name outside the four canonical dimension names is a custom dimension, kept in configured order after the canonical ones.\n\n      step_normalize_review_focus:\n        action: \"Normalize the optional operator review focus once during init\"\n        outputs:\n          - review_focus_normalized: \"Single-line focus text, or empty string when no focus was given\"\n        normalize: |\n          Collapse every control character (C0, C1, DEL, U+2028, U+2029) and whitespace run to one space, trim, treat an empty result as absent, and fail setup when more than 1000 characters remain.\n          fanout-run.cjs applies the same rule in code, so a fan-out lineage receives the same text.\n\n      step_resolve_session_id:\n        action: \"Resolve init session id from caller when supplied, else preserve timestamp fallback\"\n        branch_on: \"session_id\"\n        if_present:\n          bind:\n            session_id_init: \"{session_id}\"\n        if_absent:\n          bind:\n            session_id_init: \"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"\n\n      step_create_config:\n        action: \"Create deep-review-config.json from template with review-specific fields\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        template: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json\n        lineage_values:\n          generation_init: \"{prior_generation + 1} when lineage_mode == 'restart', else 1\"\n          lineage_mode_init: \"restart when lineage_mode == 'restart', else new\"\n          parent_session_id_init: \"{prior_session_id} when lineage_mode == 'restart', else null\"\n        populate:\n          topic: \"Review: {review_target}\"\n          mode: \"review\"\n          sessionId: \"{session_id_init}\"\n          parentSessionId: \"{parent_session_id_init}\"\n          lineageMode: \"{lineage_mode_init}\"\n          generation: \"{generation_init}\"\n          continuedFromRun: null\n          reviewTarget: \"{review_target}\"\n          reviewTargetType: \"{review_target_type}\"\n          # Reuse the single normalized init-time value from step_normalize_review_dimensions.\n          reviewDimensions: \"{review_dimensions_normalized}\"\n          # Null when review_focus_normalized is empty. The review report reads it back to show the focus.\n          reviewFocus: \"{review_focus_normalized}\"\n          resource_map_present: \"{resource_map_present}\"\n          reviewScopeFiles: \"{review_scope_files}\"\n          severityThreshold: \"P2\"\n          crossReference:\n            core: [\"spec_code\", \"checklist_evidence\"]\n            overlay: [\"skill_agent\", \"agent_cross_runtime\", \"feature_catalog_code\", \"playbook_capability\"]\n          maxIterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n          # Semantic: weighted P0/P1/P2 severity ratio. See SKILL.md §\"Convergence Threshold Semantics\".\n          convergenceThreshold: \"{convergence_threshold}\"\n          antiConvergence.convergenceMode: \"{convergence_mode}\"\n          antiConvergence.depthMode: \"{depth_mode}\"\n          # Written as a JSON integer: frontier-admit.cjs reads a quoted number as unset and falls back to the default.\n          expansiveDepth.maxDepth: \"{frontier_max_depth} when bound, else 3\"\n          expansiveDepth.maxChildrenPerNode: 6\n          expansiveDepth.budgetSplit: { depth1: 0.5, depth2: 0.35, depth3: 0.15 }\n          # Null derives the run-wide node cap at admission as half the iteration budget, so the frontier cannot claim every iteration; the depth-1 seed answers only to the root-children cap but counts toward this one. A defaulted budget is resized from the seed by step_frontier_budget so the cap keeps room past depth 1; an explicit budget is kept as given and may leave none.\n          expansiveDepth.maxFrontierNodes: \"{frontier_max_nodes} when bound, else null\"\n          antiConvergence.divergent: {}\n          stopPolicy: \"{stop_policy}\"\n          stuckThreshold: 2\n          maxDurationMinutes: 120\n          specFolder: \"{spec_folder}\"\n          # Honor the parsed --no-resource-map flag from deep-review.md:71 (default true; false when flag is set).\n          # The markdown command parses $ARGUMENTS and binds {resource_map_emit} before this step runs.\n          resource_map.emit: \"{resource_map_emit}\"\n          createdAt: \"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"\n          status: \"initialized\"\n          releaseReadinessState: \"in-progress\"\n          executionMode: \"{execution_mode}\"\n        output: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n\n      step_frontier_scope:\n        description: \"Record the files a commit-range target touches before admission reads them\"\n        enabled_when: \"depth_mode == 'expansive'\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        note: |\n          Relevance and the terminal scope gate read reviewScopeFiles, and for a\n          commit-range target only git knows those files. The command replaces the\n          list step_scope_discovery recorded with git diff --name-only <range> --\n          <pathspec>, the pathspec being the paths after '--' up to a parenthesized\n          label, and leaves any other target untouched. A fan-out lineage runs it\n          too, after its own step_create_config, so its list is the same as every\n          other lineage's. A default-mode run never reaches this step.\n        command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs scope --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\"'\n        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n        outputs:\n          - frontier_scope_json: \"The JSON line the command prints: touchedFiles, range and pathspec, or skipped\"\n        on_failure: \"Halt with the command's stderr line. Admission must not run against a guessed file list.\"\n\n      step_frontier_seed:\n        description: \"Seed the depth-1 review frontier so iteration 1 already has open nodes\"\n        enabled_when: \"depth_mode == 'expansive'\"\n        skip_when: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n        skip_reason: \"A fan-out lineage receives its share of the parent's seeded nodes from fanout-run.cjs; seeding again would duplicate them.\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        instructions: |\n          Decompose {review_target} and write {artifact_dir}/frontier-seed.json\n          exactly as the root step_frontier_seed describes, then run the command.\n          The decomposition is defined once, there; this call site exists because\n          a fan-out run seeds before phase_init and a single-executor run seeds\n          only once its config exists.\n        command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs seed --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\" --iteration 0 --input \"{artifact_dir}/frontier-seed.json\" --max-iterations-source \"{max_iterations_source}\"'\n        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n        outputs:\n          - frontier_seed_json: \"The JSON line the command prints: admitted node ids and pruned {nodeId, reason} rows\"\n        on_failure: \"Halt with the command's stderr line. A run that asked for expansive depth must not start without its seeded frontier.\"\n\n      step_frontier_budget:\n        description: \"Size a defaulted expansive budget from the seed before the loop reads max_iterations\"\n        enabled_when: \"depth_mode == 'expansive' and max_iterations_source == 'default'\"\n        skip_when: \"extension_pending == true or config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n        skip_reason: \"An explicit budget always wins, an extension already set its own budget, and a fan-out lineage gets its budget from fanout-run.cjs.\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        note: |\n          The seed decides how many nodes the frontier starts with, so a defaulted budget\n          is sized only now: min(24, max(loop default, 2 x c x (seeded nodes + maxDepth - 1))),\n          where c is 1 for research and, for review, the four canonical dimensions less\n          traceability when the configured reviewDimensions list leaves it out, plus any\n          custom name, each counted once. With no seeded node, every seed pruned,\n          the budget stays at the loop default. The node cap stays half the final budget.\n          A default-mode run never reaches this step, so its config gains no key.\n        command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs budget --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\"'\n        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n        outputs:\n          - max_iterations: \"derivedMaxIterations from the JSON output; it replaces the command default so the loop cap, the strategy and the convergence script read the same ceiling\"\n          - frontier_growth_slots: \"growthSlots from the JSON output\"\n        on_success: \"Print 'Expansive budget: <derivedMaxIterations> iterations, <growthSlots> growth slots past depth 1', and print the warning when the output carries one.\"\n        on_failure: \"Halt with the command's stderr line. The config keeps the defaulted budget.\"\n\n      step_create_state_log:\n        action: \"Open the run in the ledger: record deep_review.run_initialized through the append gateway, which writes the state log's first row\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        note: |\n          The state log is a projection the gateway rebuilds from the ledger, so this step never writes\n          it directly. A config row written beside the ledger carries keys the projection cannot\n          rebuild, and the projection refuses to drop them, so every later append in the run would\n          commit to the ledger and then exit 2. Recording the run's opening as a ledger event makes\n          the projected config row the state log's first row from the start. The full config stays\n          in deep-review-config.json, which is what the reducer reads.\n        command: |\n          GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n          [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n          EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-run-open.XXXXXX\")\"\n          node \"$(dirname \"$GATEWAY\")/workflow-steps.cjs\" run-open-review \"{state_paths.config}\" \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml\" > \"$EVENT_FILE\" || { rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"; exit 1; }\n          node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n          STATUS=$?\n          rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n          exit \"$STATUS\"\n        output: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n\n      step_record_restarted_run:\n        skip_when: \"lineage_mode != 'restart'\"\n        action: \"Record the restarted lineage after the run-open row so the restart marker never precedes deep_review.run_initialized\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.run_restarted\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}},\"data\":{\"priorTailDigest\":\"{prior_tail_digest}\",\"archivedLineageId\":\"{prior_session_id}\",\"restartReason\":\"Restart requested: the prior review packet was archived and a new lineage segment opened.\",\"continuedFromRunId\":\"{prior_session_id}-i{iteration_count}\",\"compatibilityDecision\":\"exact\",\"recoveryReceiptRef\":\"none\"}}'\n\n      step_create_findings_registry:\n        action: \"Initialize reducer-owned review findings registry\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        content: '{\"sessionId\":\"{session_id_init}\",\"generation\":{generation_init},\"lineageMode\":\"{lineage_mode_init}\",\"openFindings\":[],\"resolvedFindings\":[],\"repeatedFindings\":[],\"dimensionCoverage\":{\"correctness\":false,\"security\":false,\"traceability\":false,\"maintainability\":false{dimension_coverage_custom_seed}},\"findingsBySeverity\":{\"P0\":0,\"P1\":0,\"P2\":0},\"openFindingsCount\":0,\"resolvedFindingsCount\":0,\"convergenceScore\":0.0}'\n        output: \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n\n      step_create_strategy:\n        action: \"Create review strategy file from deep-review-strategy.md template\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        template: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md\n        populate:\n          review_target: \"{review_target}\"\n          review_target_type: \"{review_target_type}\"\n          dimensions: \"{dimension_queue}\"\n          scope_files: \"{review_scope_files}\"\n          cross_reference_targets: \"{cross_reference_targets}\"\n          max_iterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n          convergence_threshold: \"{convergence_threshold}\"\n          stop_policy: \"{stop_policy}\"\n        output: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n\n      step_seed_coverage_graph:\n        action: \"Seed the review coverage graph before the first convergence check\"\n        fanout_graph_store: 'When config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID is set, this run is a fan-out lineage and its coverage graph store is {artifact_dir}/graph-db, inside the lineage write surface. The fan-out runner exports DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR to that directory. Run this step against it and never skip it as a write outside the lineage; when DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR is absent from the environment, prefix the command with DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR=\"{artifact_dir}/graph-db\".'\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        transform: |\n          1. Convert review_scope_files into FILE nodes.\n          2. Convert review target groupings into coarse SLICE nodes only; do not expand SYMBOL\n             or DEPENDENCY nodes in review mode.\n          3. Emit COVERS edges from SLICE nodes to FILE nodes when the grouping is known.\n          4. Bind coverage_seed_source to \"scope_discovery\" and coverage_seed_confidence to 0.50.\n          5. When scope discovery yields no files, emit [] for both arrays; the upsert script\n             returns a warning and review continues with an empty graph.\n        bash: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs --spec-folder \\\"{spec_folder}\\\" --loop-type \\\"review\\\" --session-id \\\"{config.sessionId}\\\" --nodes '{coverage_seed_nodes_json}' --edges '{coverage_seed_edges_json}' --seed-source \\\"{coverage_seed_source}\\\" --seed-confidence \\\"{coverage_seed_confidence}\\\"\"\n        outputs:\n          - coverage_seed_nodes_json: \"Seed nodes for review SLICE and FILE kinds only\"\n          - coverage_seed_edges_json: \"Seed COVERS edges where review target groupings resolved\"\n          - coverage_seed_warning: \"Warning emitted when the seed batch inserts zero nodes, else empty\"\n        on_warning:\n          log: \"Coverage graph seed inserted zero nodes; continuing with an empty graph.\"\n          proceed: true\n\n      step_enrich_strategy_context:\n        action: \"Ensure Known Context is written only after strategy.md exists\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        condition: \"prior_context_found\"\n        edit: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n        note: \"Append or replace the Known Context section with prior_context_summary and retained detail from prior_context\"\n\n      step_enrich_strategy_resource_map:\n        action: \"Inject resource-map status into Known Context after strategy.md exists\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        edit: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n        note: \"When resource_map_present is true, append the resource_map_known_context snapshot and add Resource Map Coverage to the Review Charter. When false, append 'resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate'.\"\n\n      step_frontier_reduce_seed:\n        action: \"Reduce once after the seed so iteration 1 already reviews a frontier node\"\n        enabled_when: \"depth_mode == 'expansive'\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"reducer-refresh\"\n        note: \"The loop binds active_frontier_node and the frontier dimension from registry.frontier, and step_create_findings_registry writes a registry with no frontier after the seed has run. Only the reducer projects the seeded nodes into it. Without this pass the first iteration has no frontier node and no frontier block. A fan-out lineage runs it too: its reducer_artifact_arg points the reducer at the lineage's own directory, where fanout-run.cjs put its share of the nodes.\"\n        command: |\n          node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors\n        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n        on_failure: \"Log the stderr line as a config_warning bookkeeping event and continue; iteration 1 then runs on the strategy's own dimension queue and step_reduce_review_state picks the frontier up after it.\"\n\n      step_init_complete:\n        log: \"Initialization complete. Config, state, and strategy files created. Review scope: {review_scope_files_count} files, {dimension_queue_count} dimensions.\"\n        set: { current_iteration: 1, p0_count: 0, p1_count: 0, p2_count: 0 }\n\n      # ─── APPROVAL GATE: Post-Init ───\n      gate_init_approval:\n        applies_to: confirm\n        type: approval_gate\n        purpose: \"Show review scope, dimensions, and target files. Get approval to start loop.\"\n        present: |\n          ## Review Initialization Complete\n\n          **Review Target**: {review_target} ({review_target_type})\n          **Scope**: {review_scope_files_count} files\n          **Dimensions**: {dimension_queue}\n          **Max Iterations**: {max_iterations}\n          **Convergence Threshold**: {convergence_threshold}\n          **Known Context Summary**: {prior_context_summary}\n\n          **Files in scope:**\n          {review_scope_files_summary}\n\n          Review `{state_paths.strategy}` for the full scope and dimension ordering.\n          **State files located in**: {state_paths.packet_dir}/\n\n          Options:\n          A) Start review loop\n          B) Adjust scope or dimensions\n          C) Cancel\n        wait_for: \"User response\"\n        after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n        on_A: { set: { current_iteration: 1, p0_count: 0, p1_count: 0, p2_count: 0 }, proceed_to: phase_loop }\n        on_B: { action: \"Apply user adjustments to strategy.md, scope, or dimensions\", return_to: gate_init_approval }\n        on_C: { action: \"Cancel workflow\", status: \"CANCELLED\", release_lock: step_release_lock }\n\n  # ════════\n  # PHASE 2: ITERATION LOOP\n  # ════════\n","numLines":332,"startLine":100,"totalLines":431}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01S9SvuZBZPYYGxh4ZhQJWdv","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
