{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VsbRqTZws133Pqs88RJzWS","type":"tool_result","content":"---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:verification -->\n## Verification\n\n| Check | Result |\n|-------|--------|\n| Stage one, three mode requests (`skill_advisor.py … --threshold 0.5`) | `mcp-browser-use` first, 0.95, 0.93 and 0.92, `passes_threshold: true` (`scratch/after-stage1.jsonl`) |\n| Stage one, `mcp-tooling` above threshold | Still listed at 0.54 to 0.58 from generic tokens; absent under the default gate (`scratch/after-native-default-gate.txt`) |\n| Stage two, 3 mode requests, 3 tie-break requests, Lighthouse | 7 of 7 `action: route`, `selectionKind: single`, correct mode (`scratch/after-stage2.jsonl`); generic phrasing defers |\n| `compiled-route.cjs --hub mcp-browser-use` | `{\"servingAuthority\":\"legacy\"}`; admission prints `has no compiled engine registered in HUB_CHILD` |\n| Leaf maps | `keys equal: True`, `all resources exist`, Lighthouse and trace load the new leaf (`scratch/after-leaf-replay.txt`) |\n| `parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use` | `INFO: Parent skill: .skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use`, `OK: parent-skill-check — all hard invariants passed, 0 warnings` |\n| `parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/mcp-tooling` | `OK: parent-skill-check` |\n| `compiled-route-status.cjs --hub mcp-tooling`, admission | `compiled compiled-serving`; `12 pass, 0 drift` |\n| `skill_graph_validate` | `isValid: true`, 0 errors |\n23:| **Status** | Partial: REQ-002 met 2026-11-21; REQ-003 met at the default threshold but not at `--threshold 0.5`; REQ-008 held only after the browser fixtures were relabeled; REQ-009 not met as written |\n50:- Advisor vocabulary and a rebuilt graph that send browser requests to `mcp-browser-use`, with `mcp-tooling` no longer scoring them.\n61:The advisor still sends browser requests to `mcp-tooling`: a Chrome DevTools request scores `mcp-tooling` at 0.95 today. The three modes are `routingClass: metadata`, so their vocabulary reaches the advisor only through the new hub's `graph-metadata.json`, which 002 leaves without browser vocabulary, and the root `ROUTER.md` 002 writes is `stage1-only`. Until both stages name the new hub, its modes are registered but unreachable.\n75:    \"skill\": \"mcp-tooling\",\n79:$ rg -n -i 'chrome|aside|browser|mcp-tooling' .skilled/commands/doctor/mcp.md .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-mcp-install.yaml .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-mcp-debug.yaml; echo \"exit=$?\"\n82:Measured 2026-11-21. Output fields, read from a live run on `mcp-tooling` the same day: the advisor prints `skill` and `passes_threshold` per row; `compiled-route.cjs` prints `action`, `selectionKind` and `targets[].workflowMode`. Neither prints `surfaceIntents` or `intents`, so the checks below use the fields that exist. The last command above shows `/doctor:mcp`'s command doc and its two workflows name no browser mode, so this phase has no doctor work: nothing in `mcp.md`, and the mutation-guard pattern is 003's.\n91:- **Stage one (surface 6):** browser vocabulary for all three modes in `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/graph-metadata.json`, the same vocabulary removed from `.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/graph-metadata.json` (003 handed this over), and an advisor graph rebuild through `/doctor:skill-advisor`.\n97:- **Advisor fixtures:** replay the golden and labeled fixtures that assert `mcp-chrome-devtools` as a route label and confirm they still resolve under hub-membership routing (`research.md` §11). Decide whether `capture-local-native-divergence-ledger.mjs:181`, which matches `'mcp-chrome-devtools'` or `'mcp-tooling'`, also matches `mcp-browser-use` (003 handed this over).\n{\"prompt\": \"debug this page with chrome devtools and take a screenshot\", \"top3\":\n{\"prompt\": \"use aside to fill this form in my signed-in account\", \"top3\": [[\"mcp\n{\"prompt\": \"use bladebro to attach to my open browser and finish the checkout fl\n       9 specs/mcp/mc