{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J7DGAgAXh5tATsVFivABgN","type":"tool_result","content":"Detect in order, then pick the transport:\n\n```bash\ncommand -v bladebro       # binary present?\nbladebro doctor           # browser found, data root resolved, display ready?\nbladebro --version        # compare against the v4.8.2 pin before trusting any flag\n```\n\n- **CLI (default)** when `command -v bladebro` succeeds and `bladebro doctor` passes.\n- **MCP through Code Mode** with `bladebro mcp` (or `npx -y bladebro mcp`) when the binary is unavailable, or when the task needs composition with other Code Mode tools, parallel isolated sessions, or an MCP-only capability.\n- **Neither works:** report the install command and hand the decision to the operator. Never install implicitly (R-SEC-3).\n\nThe fallback is transport-driven, not capability-driven: the CLI and MCP share the same five handlers, so switching transport never adds or removes a browser capability.\n\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md:60:- **MCP through Code Mode** with `bladebro mcp` (or `npx -y bladebro mcp`) when the binary is unavailable, or when the task needs composition with other Code Mode tools, parallel isolated sessi\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/mcp-servers/bladebro-mcp/README.md:35:The registered manual is a stdio server that runs `bladebro mcp` with an empty `env`, because the server needs no credential. `BLADE_HOME` or `BLADE_FRESH` go in that \n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/feature-catalog/transport/mcp-code-mode-lane.md:26:`.utcp_config.json` carries one manual named `bladebro`: a stdio server that runs `bladebro mcp` with an empty `env`, because the server needs no credenti\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/references/mcp-wiring.md:44:The manual launches the installed binary. Without a global install, an MCP client can launch it through npm with `\"command\": \"npx\"` and `\"args\": [\"-y\", \"bladebro\", \"mcp\"]`, but \nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/001-research/research/research.md:57:| Bladebro | `command -v bladebro` → `bladebro doctor` | CLI (same five handlers as MCP) | `bladebro mcp` / `npx -y bladebro mcp` via Code Mode when chaining or th\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/004-bladebro-mode/spec.md:82:- **Lane rule (parent D2, `research.md` §4):** detect with `command -v bladebro`, then `bladebro doctor`. Use the CLI when installed. Use `bladebro mcp` (or `npx -y bladeb\n# The captures go to a scratch folder outside the repository, and the cookie step lists names only\n\nbatch_operations() {\n  local url=$1\n  shift\n  local operations=(\"$@\")\n\n  # Start session once\n  bdg \"$url\" 2>&1\n\n  # Execute all operations\n  for op in \"${operations[@]}\"; do\n    echo \"Executing: $op\"\n    eval \"$op\" 2>&1\n  done\n\n  # Stop once\n  bdg stop 2>&1\n}\n\n# Usage","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:50:22.491Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Detect in order, then pick the transport:\n\n```bash\ncommand -v bladebro       # binary present?\nbladebro doctor           # browser found, data root resolved, display ready?\nbladebro --version        # compare against the v4.8.2 pin before trusting any flag\n```\n\n- **CLI (default)** when `command -v bladebro` succeeds and `bladebro doctor` passes.\n- **MCP through Code Mode** with `bladebro mcp` (or `npx -y bladebro mcp`) when the binary is unavailable, or when the task needs composition with other Code Mode tools, parallel isolated sessions, or an MCP-only capability.\n- **Neither works:** report the install command and hand the decision to the operator. Never install implicitly (R-SEC-3).\n\nThe fallback is transport-driven, not capability-driven: the CLI and MCP share the same five handlers, so switching transport never adds or removes a browser capability.\n\n.skilled/skills/mcp-