{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DJzvPCNb5csTuNnwnmbsJF","type":"tool_result","content":"```bash\njq -c '.manual_call_templates[] | select(.name==\"bladebro\")' .utcp_config.json\n```\n\nThe manual launches the installed binary. Without a global install, an MCP client can launch it through npm with `\"command\": \"npx\"` and `\"args\": [\"-y\", \"bladebro\", \"mcp\"]`, but that pulls the package at launch, which is an install under R-SEC-3 and needs an operator yes. Set `BLADE_HOME` or `BLADE_FRESH` in `env` when a task needs isolation.\n\n---\n\n## 3. DISCOVERY BEFORE INVOCATION\n\nThe live macOS run on 2026-11-21 observed `bladebro.bladebro_{act,see,state,run,vision}` through Code Mode, and the call had to be synchronous (`return bladebro.bladebro_see({...})`); see `benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--macos-live/`. Names can change with the installed version, so confirm them each session.\n   echo 'export PATH=~/.npm-global/bin:$PATH' >> ~/.bashrc\n   source ~/.bashrc\n\n   npm install -g browser-debugger-cli@alpha\n   ```\n\n3. **Use sudo** (not recommended):\n   ```bash\n   sudo npm install -g browser-debugger-cli@alpha\n   ```\n\n---\n\n### Issue: Wrong Node version\n\n**Symptoms**:\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/SKILL.md:61:Check with `command -v bdg`, install with `npm install -g browser-debugger-cli@alpha`, then verify `bdg --version 2>&1`.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/scripts/install.sh:28:readonly MCP_PACKAGE=\"browser-debugger-cli@alpha\"\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:11:> **Package:** `browser-debugger-cli@alpha` | **Dependencies:** Node.js 20+, Chrome/Chromium\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:72:| **npm (CLI)**    | `browser-debugger-cli@alpha`                                                                |\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:80:| **CLI (bdg)**       | `browser-debugger-cli@alpha` | Single browser, quick tasks, debugging  | Lowest     |\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:101:                   (fallback)      npm i -g browser-debugger-cli@alpha","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:50:27.641Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"```bash\njq -c '.manual_call_templates[] | select(.name==\"bladebro\")' .utcp_config.json\n```\n\nThe manual launches the installed binary. Without a global install, an MCP client can launch it through npm with `\"command\": \"npx\"` and `\"args\": [\"-y\", \"bladebro\", \"mcp\"]`, but that pulls the package at launch, which is an install under R-SEC-3 and needs an operator yes. Set `BLADE_HOME` or `BLADE_FRESH` in `env` when a task needs isolation.\n\n---\n\n## 3. DISCOVERY BEFORE INVOCATION\n\nThe live macOS run on 2026-11-21 observed `bladebro.bladebro_{act,see,state,run,vision}` through Code Mode, and the call had to be synchronous (`return bladebro.bladebro_see({...})`); see `benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--macos-live/`. Names can change with the installed version, so confirm them each session.\n   echo 'export PATH=~/.npm-global/bin:$PATH' >> ~/.bashrc\n   source ~/.bashrc\n\n   npm install -g browser-debugger-cli@alpha\n   ```\n\n3. **Use sudo** (not recommended):\n   ```bash\n   sudo npm install -g browser-debugger-cli@alpha\n   ```\n\n---\n\n### Issue: Wrong Node version\n\n**Symptoms**:\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/SKILL.md:61:Check with `command -v bdg`, install with `npm install -g browser-debugger-cli@alpha`, then verify `bdg --version 2>&1`.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/scripts/install.sh:28:readonly MCP_PACKAGE=\"browser-debugger-cli@alpha\"\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:11:> **Package:** `browser-debugger-cli@alpha` | **Dependencies:** Node.js 20+, Chrome/Chromium\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:72:| **npm (CLI)**    | `browser-debugger-cli@alpha`                                                                |\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:80:| **CLI (bdg)**       | `browser-debugger-cli@alpha` | Single browser, quick tasks, debugging  | Lowest     |\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:101:                   (fallback)      npm i -g browser-debugger-cli@alpha","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DJzvPCNb5csTuNnwnmbsJF","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
