{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DWTn4aSMmAc5L2EJJDf5M6","type":"tool_result","content":"-**UNKNOWN — model-flag spelling**: docs show `-m provider/model` while the installed help shows separate `--model` and `--provider` options. Unresolved; capture the installed version's help before using either spelling.\n+**Model-flag spelling**: on 1.26.626.1517 the installed help defines `-m, --model <model>` (it also accepts `provider/model`) and `-p, --provider <provider>`, so `-m provider/model` and `--model <id> --provider <name>` both work. Capture the installed version's help before scripting flags.\n+**Browser-profile binding**: on 1.26.626.1517, with the Aside app running and signed in, a fresh `aside mcp` process is bound and `listBrowserTabs()` returns tabs (ASD-010). Earlier versions left a fresh process browser-unbound, and `listBrowserTabs()` failed with \"This task is not bound to a browser profile.\" Other states, such as the app closed, are untested. When that error appears, it is a binding failure, not an auth failure. The supported binding procedure is **UNKNOWN** (undocumented); report it distinctly and stop.\n+6. A needed flag is missing from the installed version's `--help`.\n--- a/.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/changelog/v1.0.27.0.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/changelog/v1.0.27.0.md\n-In bdg 0.6.10, `bdg dom eval` only finds the session's tab when the session runs on port 9222. On any other port it exits with code 83 and prints `Session target not found`, even though the tab is open. The troubleshoot\n+bdg 0.6.10 has a port defect in `bdg dom eval` and in the form commands `dom click`, `dom fill`, `dom submit` and `dom pressKey`. They find the session's tab only on port 9222. On any other port they exit with code 83. \n-- A new entry in `references/troubleshooting.md` §6 shows the error, its cause and a check for the session's port.\n-- The first fix starts the session without `-p`, so it uses 9222, when that port is free.\n-- The second fix reads page values with `bdg cdp Runtime.evaluate --params '{…,\"returnByValue\":true}'`, which works on any session port.\n-- The guide is now version 1.0.5.0 and adds \"session target not found\" to its trigger phrases.\n+- A new entry in `references/troubleshooting.md` §6 shows the error and its cause. It also shows how to check the session's port.\n+- The first fix starts the session without `-p` when 9222 is free. The session then uses 9222. It is the only fix for the form commands, which take no `-p` option.\n+- The second fix reads page values with `bdg cdp Runtime.evaluate --params '{…,\"returnByValue\":true}'`. That works on any session port. It reads values only and gives no route for a click or a fill.\n+- The guide is now version 1.0.5.0. Its trigger phrases now include \"session target not found\".\n3395b32f6b1 2026-11-22 fix(sk-doc): accept --reports only for the skill or its hub\na5d1912a6c2 2026-11-22 feat(mcp-browser-use): give Bladebro an install guide, manual asset and scripts\ne60f28021d1 2026-11-21 refactor(mcp-browser-use): move the Chrome DevTools and Aside modes into the browser hub\n103:| `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/**` | Modify | References, install docs, README, SKILL, catalog, playbook, changelog, scripts and examples |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:53:49.851Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"-**UNKNOWN — model-flag spelling**: docs show `-m provider/model` while the installed help shows separate `--model` and `--provider` options. Unresolved; capture the installed version's help before using either spelling.\n+**Model-flag spelling**: on 1.26.626.1517 the installed help defines `-m, --model <model>` (it also accepts `provider/model`) and `-p, --provider <provider>`, so `-m provider/model` and `--model <id> --provider <name>` both work. Capture the installed version's help before scripting flags.\n+**Browser-profile binding**: on 1.26.626.1517, with the Aside app running and signed in, a fresh `aside mcp` process is bound and `listBrowserTabs()` returns tabs (ASD-010). Earlier versions left a fresh process browser-unbound, and `listBrowserTabs()` failed with \"This task is not bound to a browser profile.\" Other states, such as the app closed, are untested. When that error appears, it is a binding failure, not an auth failure. The supported binding procedure is **UNKNOWN** (undocumented); report it distinctly and stop.\n+6. A needed flag is missing from the installed version's `--help`.\n--- a/.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/changelog/v1.0.27.0.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/changelog/v1.0.27.0.md\n-In bdg 0.6.10, `bdg dom eval` only finds the session's tab when the session runs on port 9222. On any other port it exits with code 83 and prints `Session target not found`, even though the tab is open. The troubleshoot\n+bdg 0.6.10 has a port defect in `bdg dom eval` and in the form commands `dom click`, `dom fill`, `dom submit` and `dom pressKey`. They find the session's tab only on port 9222. On any other port they exit with code 83. \n-- A new entry in `references/troubleshooting.md` §6 shows the error, its cause and a check for the session's port.\n-- The first fix starts the session without `-p`, so it uses 9222, when that port is free.\n-- The second fix reads page values with `bdg cdp Runtime.evaluate --params '{…,\"returnByValue\":true}'`, which works on any session port.\n-- The guide is now version 1.0.5.0 and adds \"session target not found\" to its trigger phrases.\n+- A new entry in `references/troubleshooting.md` §6 shows the error and its cause. It also shows how to check the session's port.\n+- The first fix starts the session without `-p` when 9222 is free. The session then uses 9222. It is the only fix for the form commands, which take no `-p` option.\n+- The second fix reads page values with `bdg cdp Runtime.evaluate --params '{…,\"returnByValue\":true}'`. That works on any session port. It reads values only and gives no route for a click or a fill.\n+- The guide is now version 1.0.5.0. Its trigger phrases now include \"session target not found\".\n3395b32f6b1 2026-11-22 fix(sk-doc): accept --reports only for the skill or its hub\na5d1912a6c2 2026-11-22 feat(mcp-browser-use): give Bladebro an install guide, manual asset and scripts\ne60f28021d1 2026-11-21 refactor(mcp-browser-use): move the Chrome DevTools and Aside modes into the browser hub\n103:| `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/**` | Modify | References, install docs, README, SKILL, catalog, playbook, changelog, scripts and examples |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[],"moreFiles":0,"unavailable":true}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DWTn4aSMmAc5L2EJJDf5M6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
