{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Uou9qqGogiEwPBHpZF457t","type":"tool_result","content":"// less traceability plus every custom name, so a list naming a canonical subset\n// still holds a node open for, and dispatches it to, the canonical names it omits.\nfunction reviewOmitsTraceability(config) {\n  const dimensions = config ? config.reviewDimensions : undefined;\n  return Array.isArray(dimensions) && !dimensions.includes('traceability');\n}\n\n// Its cross-reference protocols are not owed at stop when traceability is left out.\nfunction reviewTraceabilityCovered(config, registry) {\n  if (reviewOmitsTraceability(config)) {\n    return true;\n  }\n  const traceability = isPlainObject(registry.traceability) ? registry.traceability : {};\n  const summary = isPlainObject(traceability.summary) ? traceability.summary : null;\n  const core = isPlainObject(config.crossReference) && Array.isArray(config.crossReference.core)\n    ? config.crossReference.core\n    : [];\n  const settingsPassed = summary !== null ? summary.gatingFailures === 0 : core.length === 0;\n  if (!settingsPassed) return false;\n\n  const results = Array.isArray(traceability.results) ? traceability.results : [];\n  const incompleteStatuses = new Set(['', 'pending', 'deferred', 'skipped']);\n  return core.every((id) => results.some((entry) => {\n    if (!isPlainObject(entry) || entry.protocolId !== id) return false;\n    if (typeof entry.status !== 'string') return false;\n    return !incompleteStatuses.has(entry.status.toLowerCase());\n  }));\n}\n\n// The core protocols a stop still owes. A review that reaches its iteration cap\n// before every veto has run closes over a partial verdict, so the ids are\n// reported as a stop input and the last iteration can be steered to them.\nfunction reviewUnfinishedCoreProtocols(config, registry) {\n  const core = isPlainObject(config?.crossReference) && Array.isArray(config.crossReference.core)\n    ? config.crossReference.core\n    : [];\n  if (core.length === 0) return [];\n\n  const traceability = isPlainObject(registry?.traceability) ? registry.traceability : {};\n  const results = Array.isArray(traceability.results) ? traceability.results : [];\n  const latestStatusById = new Map();\n1680:function reviewCoverageAge(evidenceRecords, dimensions) {\n1681-  if (dimensions.length === 0) return 0;\n1682-  const covered = new Set();\n1683-  for (let index = 0; index < evidenceRecords.length; index += 1) {\n1684-    const record = evidenceRecords[index];\n1685-    if (Array.isArray(record.dimensions)) {\n1686-      for (const dimension of record.dimensions) covered.add(dimension);\n1687-    }\n1688-    if (dimensions.every((dimension) => covered.has(dimension))) {\n1689-      return evidenceRecords.length - 1 - index;\n1690-    }\n1691-  }\n1692-  return 0;\n1693-}\n1694-\n1695-// A run configured with a dimension list that leaves traceability out never\n1696-// reviews it. An absent list means the default four, which include traceability.\n1697-// The stop gate and the reducer's dimension universe share this one test, so\n1698-// neither owes traceability when the list leaves it out. They share nothing else:\n1699-// the stop owes the configured list, while a frontier node owes the canonical four\n1700-// less traceability plus every custom name, so a list naming a canonical subset\n1701-// still holds a node open for, and dispatches it to, the canonical names it omits.\n1702-function reviewOmitsTraceability(config) {","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:55:04.432Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"// less traceability plus every custom name, so a list naming a canonical subset\n// still holds a node open for, and dispatches it to, the canonical names it omits.\nfunction reviewOmitsTraceability(config) {\n  const dimensions = config ? config.reviewDimensions : undefined;\n  return Array.isArray(dimensions) &