{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014XaSKkzMV7X2faS1AysMmd","type":"tool_result","content":"      step_handle_convergence:\n        action: \"Act on convergence decision\"\n        if_consecutive_failures:\n          applies_to: confirm\n          when: \"stop_decision.reasonDetail == 'consecutiveFailures'. This branch runs instead of if_stop.\"\n          gate_consecutive_failures:\n            type: approval_gate\n            purpose: \"In confirm mode, ask the operator Retry / Skip / Cancel before synthesis starts.\"\n            present: |\n              **{consecutive_failure_count} iterations in a row failed.**\n\n              Options:\n              A) Retry: dispatch the next iteration with the same dimension\n              B) Skip: dispatch the next iteration with the next dimension\n              C) Cancel: end the run with no synthesis\n            wait_for: \"User response\"\n            after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n            on_A: { set: { decision: \"CONTINUE\" }, proceed_to: step_normalize_pause_events }\n            on_B: { action: \"Advance next_dimension to the next uncovered dimension in strategy.md\", set: { decision: \"CONTINUE\" }, proceed_to: step_normalize_pause_events }\n            on_C: { action: \"Cancel workflow\", status: \"CANCELLED\", release_lock: step_release_lock }\n          note: \"The failure count is rebuilt from the state log, so this gate asks again after each further failed iteration and stops asking once an iteration completes.\"\n        if_stop:\n          record_terminal_gates:\n            when: \"Run once, immediately before control jumps to phase_synthesis: in if_existing_terminal_path, in the divergent pivot's if_failed and on_error branches, and in every confirm-mode manualStop exit (on_C) into phase_synthesis: both divergent pivot gates, gate_pre_iteration and the post-iteration gate. The auto three-errors stop (reason error) reaches it through if_existing_terminal_path. The duration stop in step_check_max_duration runs it, once, before its jump to phase_synthesis.\n            bash: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/terminal-gates.cjs --config-path \"{state_paths.config}\" --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" --registry-path \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"'\n            note: \"The script computes all three gates from the config, state log and registry: evidence by the evidenceDensityGate rule, coverage by the dimensionCoverageGate rule, and scope by matching every open finding's file against reviewScopeFiles. Never judge a gate from the findings yourself. Run it fresh at this stop, even when an earlier blocked stop recorded failures.\"\n            on_error: \"When the script exits non-zero or prints status error, fail closed: bind terminal_gate_results_json to three rows, evidence, scope and coverage, each with status fail, reasonCode gate-script-error and evidenceDigest the sha256 of the script's error text, and bind failed_required_gate_ids to [\\\"evidence\\\",\\\"scope\\\",\\\"coverage\\\"].\"\n            evaluate: |\n              terminal_stop_reason = reason when it is maxIterationsReached, maxDurationReached, manualStop or error; blockedStop when decision is STOP and reason is blockedStop; else \"converged\". Read reason, never stopReason: every manual stop sets reason to manualStop while stopReason may still hold blockedStop or stuckRecovery\n            outputs:\n              - terminal_gate_results_json: \"Tool terminal_gate_results_json: three rows {gateId, status, reasonCode, evidenceDigest} in the order evidence, scope, coverage\"\n              - failed_required_gate_ids: \"Tool failed_required_gate_ids: the gateIds whose status is fail, in that order; [] when all pass\"\n              - terminal_stop_reason: \"From evaluate\"\n            append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.terminal_gates_recorded\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation},\"iterationId\":\"iteration-{current_iteration}\"},\"data\":{\"stopReason\":\"{terminal_stop_reason}\",\"gateResults\":{terminal_gate_results_json},\"failedRequiredGateIds\":{failed_required_gate_ids},\"appendPosition\":{current_iteration}}}'\n            log: \"Terminal gates recorded at stop {terminal_stop_reason}. Failed required gates: {failed_required_gate_ids}\"\n          branch_on: \"convergence_mode == 'divergent' AND stop_decision.reasonDetail == 'all_dimensions_clean'\"\n          if_divergent_eligible:\n            eligibility_contract:\n              required_decision: \"STOP\"\n              eligible_reasons: [all_dimensions_clean]\n              excluded_reasons: [maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, error, manualStop, userPaused, maxDurationReached]\n              fail_closed: \"Any missing or ambiguous reason uses if_existing_terminal_path without preparing a pivot. The nine legal-stop gates have already run and remain unchanged.\"\n              frontier_gate: \"Under depth_mode == 'expansive' the pivot is eligible only once registry.frontier holds no open or active node. The frontierOpen stop veto already returns CONTINUE while one is open, so this gate records the order rather than adding a second check. A candidate the pivot accepts becomes next_dimension through pivot_result.restoredFocus; with the frontier terminal the leaf gets no FRONTIER block, so the pivot adds no frontier node. The pivot may seed from nodes closed\n            steps:\n                      proceed_to: step_normalize_pause_events\n                    on_C:\n                      bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"manualStop\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"stopReason\":\"manualStop\",\"pivotId\":\"{pivot_result.pivotId}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}}'\n                      set: { reason: \"manualStop\" }\n                      run_first: record_terminal_gates\n                      skip_to: phase_synthesis\n                  run_first: record_terminal_gates\n                  log: \"Divergent review pivot {pivot_result.pivotId} failed closed ({pivot_result.failureReason}); proceeding to synthesis.\"\n                  skip_to: phase_synthesis\n            on_error:\n              run_first: record_terminal_gates\n              log: \"Divergent review pivot integration error; failing closed to the existing synthesis path.\"\n              skip_to: phase_synthesis\n          if_existing_terminal_path:\n            run_first: record_terminal_gates\n            log: \"Loop stopping. Reason: {reason}\"\n            skip_to: phase_synthesis\n        if_blocked:","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T05:02:00.567Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"      step_handle_convergence:\n        action: \"Act on convergence decision\"\n        if_consecutive_failures:\n          applies_to: confirm\n          when: \"stop_decision.reasonDetail == 'consecutiveFailures'. This branch runs instead of if_stop.\"\n          gate_consecutive_failures:\n            type: approval_gate\n            purpose: \"In confirm mode, ask the operator Retry / Skip / Cancel before synthesis starts.\"\n            present: |\n              **{consecutive_failure_count} iterations in a row failed.**\n\n              Options:\n              A) Retry: dispatch the next iteration with the same dimension\n              B) Skip: dispatch the next iteration with the next dimension\n              C) Cancel: end the run with no synthesis\n            wait_for: \"User response\"\n            after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n            on_A: { set: { decision: \"CONTINUE\" }, proceed_to: step_normalize_pause_events }\n            on_B: { action: \"Advance next_dimension to the next uncovered dimension in strategy.md\", 