{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChMAcoozBPdpgpXRpH7Ts","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0129s4ZcC4R9PXb1d8VUwizN","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled; L=specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/review/lineages/opus-3; cat > $L/.work/fixrep.cjs <<'EOF'\nconst fs=require(\"fs\");const p=process.argv[2];let t=fs.readFileSync(p,\"utf8\");\nconst rep=(a,b)=>{if(!t.includes(a))throw new Error(\"missing: \"+a.slice(0,60));t=t.replace(a,b);};\nrep(\"- **Overall verdict: CONDITIONAL**\\n- hasAdvisories: false. The verdict is CONDITIONAL, and the flag only applies to PASS.\",\n\"- **Overall verdict: FAIL**. No P0 exists. The FAIL comes from a required quality gate still failing at the terminal stop: `terminal-gates.cjs` reports evidence pass, scope pass, **coverage fail** (`traceability-incomplete`), because the hard core protocol `checklist_evidence` stayed partial through iteration 7. On findings alone the verdict would be CONDITIONAL (two active P1).\\n- hasAdvisories: false. The flag only applies to PASS.\");\nrep(\"- Active counts the verdict used (from `review-verdict.cjs` over the registry): **P0 0, P1 2, P2 8**\",\"- Active counts the verdict used (from `review-verdict.cjs` over the registry): **P0 0, P1 2, P2 8**, `failed_required_gate_ids: [\\\"coverage\\\"]`\");\nrep(\"`/speckit:plan` is required: two active P1 findings.\",\"`/speckit:plan` is required: a failed coverage gate plus two active P1 findings. The coverage gate clears once the goal-state drifts behind `checklist_evidence` are reconciled (WS-5) and a follow-up review records the protocol as pass.\");\nrep(\"\\\"verdict\\\": \\\"CONDITIONAL\\\",\",\"\\\"verdict\\\": \\\"FAIL\\\",\\n  \\\"failedRequiredGateIds\\\": [\\\"coverage\\\"],\");\nrep(\"Dimension coverage reached 4/4 at iteration 4. `checklist_evidence` stayed partial, so the coverage gate held and the stop reason is `maxIterationsReached` at 7/7.\",\"Dimension coverage reached 4/4 at iteration 4. `checklist_evidence` stayed partial, so the coverage gate held and the stop reason is `maxIterationsReached` at 7/7.\\n- Terminal gates (recorded late, after the `synthesis_complete` row, because the stop branch's `record_terminal_gates` step was first skipped and then run at closeout): evidence pass, scope pass, coverage fail. The `synthesis_complete` ledger row carries the earlier CONDITIONAL verdict. The ledger is append-only, so the registry's `terminalGates` plus `review-verdict.cjs` (FAIL) are the record.\\n- Registry note: R7-P2-001 was recorded with `refines: R6-P2-001`, so the registry folds both into one P2 entry carrying R7's title on R6's file. The two defects (understated REQ-009 note, `rb` alias overreach) are described separately in section 3.\");\nfs.writeFileSync(p,t);\nEOF\nnode $L/.work/fixrep.cjs $L/review-report.md && grep -n \"Overall verdict\\|\\\"verdict\\\"\" $L/review-report.md | cut -c1-120; rm -rf $L/.work; ls -a $L | grep -c work","description":"Update report verdict to FAIL and clean temp"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1376,"cache_read_input_tokens":268257,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1376},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T05:02:34.156Z","request_id":"<redacted>","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0129s4ZcC4R9PXb1d8VUwizN":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled; L=specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/review/lineages/opus-3; cat > $L/.work/fixrep.cjs <<'EOF'\nconst fs=require(\"fs\");const p=process.argv[2];let t=fs.readFileSync(p,\"utf8\");\nconst rep=(a,b)=>{if(!t.includes(a))throw new Error(\"missing: \"+a.slice(0,60));t=t.replace(a,b);};\nrep(\"- **Overall verdict: CONDITIONAL**\\n- hasAdvisories: false. The verdict is CONDITIONAL, and the flag only applies to PASS.\",\n\"- **Overall verdict: FAIL**. No P0 exists. The FAIL comes from a required quality gate still failing at the terminal stop: `terminal-gates.cjs` reports evidence pass, scope pass, **coverage fail** (`traceability-incomplete`), because the hard core protocol `checklist_evidence` stayed partial through iteration 7. On findings alone the verdict would be CONDITIONAL (two active P1).\\n- hasAdvisories: false. The flag only applies to PASS.\");\nrep(\"- Active counts the verdict used (from `review-verdict.cjs` over the registry): **P0 0, P1 2, P2 8**\",\"- Active counts the verdict used (from `review-verdict.cjs` over the registry): **P0 0, P1 2, P2 8**, `failed_required_gate_ids: [\\\"coverage\\\"]`\");\nrep(\"`/speckit:plan` is required: two active P1 findings.\",\"`/speckit:plan` is required: a failed coverage gate plus two active P1 findings. The coverage gate clears once the goal-state drifts behind `checklist_evidence` are reconciled (WS-5) and a follow-up review records the protocol as pass.\");\nrep(\"\\\"verdict\\\": \\\"CONDITIONAL\\\",\",\"\\\"verdict\\\": \\\"FAIL\\\",\\n  \\\"failedRequiredGateIds\\\": [\\\"coverage\\\"],\");\nrep(\"Dimension coverage reached 4/4 at iteration 4. `checklist_evidence` stayed partial, so the coverage gate held and the stop reason is `maxIterationsReached` at 7/7.\",\"Dimension coverage reached 4/4 at iteration 4. `checklist_evidence` stayed partial, so the coverage gate held and the stop reason is `maxIterationsReached` at 7/7.\\n- Terminal gates (recorded late, after the `synthesis_complete` row, because the stop branch's `record_terminal_gates` step was first skipped and then run at closeout): evidence pass, scope pass, coverage fail. The `synthesis_complete` ledger row carries the earlier CONDITIONAL verdict. The ledger is append-only, so the registry's `terminalGates` plus `review-verdict.cjs` (FAIL) are the record.\\n- Registry note: R7-P2-001 was recorded with `refines: R6-P2-001`, so the registry folds both into one P2 entry carrying R7's title on R6's file. The two defects (understated REQ-009 note, `rb` alias overreach) are described separately in section 3.\");\nfs.writeFileSync(p,t);\nEOF\nnode $L/.work/fixrep.cjs $L/review-report.md && grep -n \"Overall verdict\\|\\\"verdict\\\"\" $L/review-report.md | cut -c1-120; rm -rf $L/.work; ls -a $L | grep -c work","description":"Update report verdict to FAIL and clean temp"}}}
