{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChMAdtVnvehov741LA3fd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The opus-3 lineage finished: 7 of 7 iterations, all recorded through the append gateway and reduced. Its verdict is **FAIL**. There is no P0. The FAIL comes from the coverage gate, which was still failing when the loop stopped at the iteration cap. On findings alone the verdict would be CONDITIONAL.\n\n**Why the gate fails:** `terminal-gates.cjs` reports evidence pass, scope pass, coverage fail (`traceability-incomplete`). The required `checklist_evidence` check stayed partial through iteration 7. Phases 003 and 004 are marked Complete with every goal box unticked. Phase 005's goal is fully ticked while its spec says Partial. Phase 011's count check no longer reproduces.\n\n**Active findings: P0 0, P1 2, P2 8**\n- **P1:** Phase 013 changed only the Chrome DevTools copy of `_utils.sh` (the Node minimum went from 18 to 20). `.skilled/bin/tests/mcp-installers.test.cjs` now fails its \"both copies identical\" test, so phase 003's criterion that this test exits 0 is false.\n- **P1:** `mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md:60` offers `npx -y bladebro mcp` when the binary is missing, with no operator yes. That pulls an unpinned, unchecked package, which the file's own R-SEC-3 forbids at line 116.\n- **P2s:**\n  - Chrome DevTools installs `browser-debugger-cli@alpha` while the docs are aligned to bdg 0.6.10.\n  - Phase 013 changed scripts in two packets without cutting a release: it rewrote 011's published v1.0.27.0 note and gave Aside no entry.\n  - Tie-break routing passes only on the recorded phrasings, just above the 0.8 floor; plain rewordings return nothing.\n  - Half of 005's out-of-domain test phrases still reach the hub above 0.8, more than its note admits, and the `rb status`/`rb attach` aliases route Ruby prompts to Bladebro.\n  - Goal and spec drift: the 003/004 goal boxes, 005's ticked criterion 1, 011's count, and a \"TBD\" handoff row in the parent `spec.md`.\n\n**What still holds:** most of the other runnable goal criteria reproduce on the current tree. That includes the registry counts, the stale-path greps, the parent-skill checks, the mutation guard, the playbook and catalog validators, the recorded-run tallies and all six recorded two-stage routing requests.\n\n**Deviations you should know about:**\n- I skipped `record_terminal_gates` when the loop stopped and recorded it later, after the `synthesis_complete` row. That row still says CONDITIONAL and can't be rewritten, since the ledger is append-only. The registry and `review-verdict.cjs` both give FAIL, and `review-report.md` now matches.\n- Iteration 7's finding was recorded as a refinement of iteration 6's, so the registry folds two separate defects into one P2 entry. The report describes them separately.\n- The recorded finding details lack the `scopeProof` and `affectedSurfaceHints` fields. They are in the iteration files, but the ledger can't be amended.\n- A few writes landed outside the lineage directory:\n  - a temp file in `/tmp`, created and deleted in iteration 6;\n  - temp directories made by the two test suites I ran;\n  - gitignored advisor daemon files (heartbeat, lease) touched by the advisor calls.\n- No tracked file outside the lineage changed.\n- Not checked here, because the lineage contract bars `validate.sh`: the parent's criterion 7 and the `validate.sh --recursive` criteria in phases 009–013.\n\nThe report is at `specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/review/lineages/opus-3/review-report.md`.\n\nFANOUT_LINEAGE_COMPLETE:opus-3"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1729,"cache_read_input_tokens":269633,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1729},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformation